Usage: nfa [FILE ...]

Options:
    help                    Print this help text and exit
    reg REGEX               Creates an automaton based on
                            the regular expression.
                            (constraints: integers and
                            lowercase latin letters)
    save ID FILE            Save the automaton in the file
    open FILE [FILE ...]    Load the listed automatons in
                            the listed automatons
    close ID [ID ...]       Remove automatons from memory
    close *                 Removes all automatons from
                            memory
    list                    Lists all automatons in memory
    print ID                Prints all transitions of said
                            automaton
    empty ID                Checks if the automaton's
                            language is empty
    deterministic ID        Checks if the automaton is
                            deterministic
    recognize ID word       Returns true if the automaton
                            recognizes the word
    concat ID ID [ID ...]   Creates new automaton that is
                            concatenation of all listed
                            automatons. Order is important -
                            second automaton is concatenated
                            to the first and so on.
    union ID ID [ID ...]    Creates a new automaton that
                            is the union of all listed
                            automatons
    un ID                   Creates an automaton that is
                            applied Kleene plus on
                            said automaton
    exit                    Exits the program